 callback time charged to the drain. They use mocks plus one small managed source
 file hash; no observer native type, compiler, process, lease or game is launched.
 
+## Source-only closure proposal after v5
+
+The v5 native run also remains a global failure: all build/test/binder steps passed,
+but the two-second original-job drain expired. Its diagnostic captured one original
+job member at the pinned MSVC sibling `vctip.exe` path, SHA256
+`d591358c6aee4b673562ca3b3a15c250e612708394fe3b44a7a7eda2470570a5`, 335288 bytes.
+The parent PID was recorded; parent process identity and compiler ancestry were not.
+The original job was then stopped, closure confirmed and the lease released. The
+immutable supervision SHA256 is `2060bdc7c829ce458810e5de2ca36b3ab28e304e6df7a51e9d0d6ac9362cc36a`.
+
+See [the proposed closure contract](residual-closure-contract.md) for the Microsoft
+documentation findings, required positive completion/identity/guard/closure evidence
+and remaining implementation gate. `residual_policy.ps1` implements only the pure
+identity predicate with 96 synthetic checks. It authorizes no action and is not
+imported by the launcher. Existing 100 supervision/registration/diagnostic checks
+and four Python preparation tests still pass. No new Plan or native run was made.
+
 ```text
 python -B audit/prepare.py --output build/identity-reviewed
 cmake -S audit -B build/audit-native -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64 -DAUDIT_IDENTITY_DIR=ABSOLUTE_IDENTITY_DIRECTORY
